Smart Event and Concert Booking System

1. Risk Identification

I. Risk Identification

The main risks identified for the Smart Event and Concert Booking System are:

1. Server Failure – The application may become unavailable if the cloud server or backend service fails during event browsing or ticket booking.

2. Cybersecurity Attack – Unauthorized access, data breaches, or attacks may affect user accounts, booking records, and payment-related information.

3. Payment Gateway Failure – Failure, timeout, or delay in the third-party payment gateway may interrupt ticket purchases and cause payment or booking inconsistencies.

4. Double Booking of Seats – Multiple users may attempt to book the same seat simultaneously, resulting in incorrect seat allocation or duplicate bookings.

5. Network Outage – Internet connection failure may affect event browsing, seat selection, payment verification, and ticket delivery.

6. Database/Data Loss – Database failure or data loss may affect user accounts, event details, seat availability, booking records, and ticket information.

7. QR Code / Ticket Generation Failure – Failure in generating PDF tickets or QR codes may prevent customers from receiving valid digital entry passes.

8. Incorrect Seat Availability Data – Incorrect or outdated seat status may cause users to select unavailable seats or prevent valid bookings.

9. Promo Code Error – Incorrect discount calculations or invalid promo code handling may result in wrong ticket prices or financial loss.

10. Email Notification Failure – Failure of the email notification service may prevent customers from receiving booking confirmations and digital tickets.

