IV. Risk Mitigation Strategies

Risk| Mitigation Strategy
Server failure| Use reliable cloud servers, backup servers, health monitoring, and regular maintenance.
Cybersecurity attack| Use HTTPS, bcrypt password hashing, role-based access control, secure database practices, and input validation.
Payment gateway failure| Use a reliable payment gateway, handle payment timeouts, maintain transaction status logs, and provide a retry option.
Double booking of seats| Implement temporary seat locking, server-side seat availability validation, database transactions, and concurrency control.
Network outage| Display suitable error messages, preserve booking state where possible, and prevent false payment or booking confirmation.
Database/data loss| Perform regular backups, maintain secure database storage, and test database restoration procedures.
QR code/ticket generation failure| Validate ticket generation, store booking references securely, and allow confirmed users to retrieve their digital tickets.
Incorrect seat availability data| Validate seat status on the server, synchronize seat availability, and prevent selection of sold or locked seats.
Promo code error| Validate promo codes, check expiry and eligibility, and verify discount calculations before payment.
Email notification failure| Use reliable email services, maintain delivery logs, and provide an in-platform ticket download option.

